{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Agartli</b> — sprinkling bowls. Its meaning in the Yerushalmi: why are they called agartli? Because they gather there the blood of the lamb. [The word has] thirty-two [or: של\"א] letters [or: forms] from the end of the book." "<b>Agartli</b> — the word is quinary [five letters], or the alef is added and its meaning is goblets. מחלפים — knives, and it is from the root of כליל יחלוף, בני חלוף, whose sense is cutting."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase 'של\"א מ\"ן הספ\"ר' is obscure. It may involve a numerical or abbreviation notation (של\"א = 331; מ\"ן = 90; ספ\"ר = 280/340 depending on form), but its sense here is uncertain and possibly corrupt. Translated hyper-literally.", 1 "No note needed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:34.062572857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}